(OPR-40 (undocumented precision): the comparison operators of
 LANGUAGE.md:4810-4817 are not first-class expressions. A comparison
 parses only in a condition position (an If/but-if/while condition);
 printing one, or binding one to a boolean, is a compile error. The
 arithmetic and bitwise operators have no such restriction. Nothing in
 the Operators section says the two tables differ this way.
 (Compile-error claim: not assertable from a runtime leaf.)
